            "topic": "Failure behavior",
            "choice": "Use the shared boundary taxonomy: `unauthorized`, `forbidden`, `upstream`, `network`, `contract`, or `unknown`.",
            "rationale": "The boundary reports once and the RSC adapter translates the classified result; raw database/provider errors never reach the UI."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Inaccessible labels",
            "choice": "Fail the whole board read with `forbidden` when a non-archived item references a label the actor cannot view.",
            "rationale": "This explicitly enforces the requirement and prevents silently presenting an incomplete or misleading board."
          },
